    {
      "id": "I_kwDOKIwiaM7hVk2-",
      "title": "Mismatch description for batcher configuration variable `max-blocks-per-span-batc`",
      "author": "NIC619",
      "number": 1933,
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/docs",
      "body": "The configuration variable `max-blocks-per-span-batch` has the description and example of a different configuration variable `check-recent-txs-depth`\n\n<img width=\"748\" height=\"260\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d0817253-aa8b-49f0-a580-9d610e0fcf50\" />\n\nPath: /chain-operators/guides/configuration/batcher",
      "createdAt": "2026-01-05T07:56:35Z",
      "closedAt": null,
      "state": "OPEN",
      "commentCount": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "I_kwDOKIwiaM7hjKRu",
      "title": "New landing page",
      "author": "sbvegan",
      "number": 1936,
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/docs",
      "body": "<!-- please fill out the description and acceptance criteria to the best of your ability. While the other sections are optional, it makes resolving the issue much easier. -->\n\n## Description \n<!-- Write a clear and concise description of the docs request. For example, is the request related to an existing page or are you suggesting a brand-new docs page? -->\nWe're going to need a new landing page that directs developer to their correct area of interest. Currently it just points you to how to launch a chain. Instead it should guide users to different sections of the documentation for chain operators, node operators, protocol information, superchain information, governance stuff, and protocol notices.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n<!-- Clearly list out the definition of done. -->\n\n## User stories\n<!-- User stories that illustrate the benefits of this issue. For example, this documentation improvement will allow user X to be able to Y. -->\nAs a developer, I should be pointed to the area of interest so I get accomplish a goal that I set out to do or to learn more about a specific area.\n\n\n## Resources and support\n<!-- Provide additional documentation, context, and subject matter experts to help us complete this issue. -->\nWe should lean on our design team to help us out here to get something minimal out the door\n\n## Action items\n<!-- Clear steps to take to complete this issue -->\n",
      "createdAt": "2026-01-06T07:34:10Z",
      "closedAt": null,
      "state": "OPEN",
      "commentCount": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "I_kwDOKIwiaM7hjFx2",
      "title": "Clarify the pebble db path vs hash state scheme",
      "author": "sbvegan",
      "number": 1935,
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/docs",
      "body": "<!-- please fill out the description and acceptance criteria to the best of your ability. While the other sections are optional, it makes resolving the issue much easier. -->\n\n## Description \n<!-- Write a clear and concise description of the docs request. For example, is the request related to an existing page or are you suggesting a brand-new docs page? -->\n- Internally we have confirmed pebble/path works with full nodes, but we haven't really tested archive pebble/path nodes. All of our full nodes are configured that way.\n- However we don't run any archive pebble/path nodes currently because they don't support all the functionality we need for archive rpc (specifically eth_getProof for historical blocks)\n\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n<!-- Clearly list out the definition of done. -->\n\n## User stories\n<!-- User stories that illustrate the benefits of this issue. For example, this documentation improvement will allow user X to be able to Y. -->\n\n\n## Resources and support\n<!-- Provide additional documentation, context, and subject matter experts to help us complete this issue. -->\n- [Slack thread](https://oplabs-pbc.slack.com/archives/CQZ0U9FAN/p1765999321444599)\n\n## Action items\n<!-- Clear steps to take to complete this issue -->\n- Maybe add this information here: https://docs.optimism.io/chain-operators/reference/architecture or likely take information from that page and put more stuff in here: https://docs.optimism.io/chain-operators/guides/management/best-practices\n",
      "createdAt": "2026-01-06T07:27:23Z",
      "closedAt": null,
      "state": "OPEN",
      "commentCount": 0
    },
